{% comment %}
  The cross-sell map behind the cart drawer's recommendation rail, transcribed from the
  merchandising sheet:
  https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13_P5FifrhZOnngJqmBPxGkVt5B45BR3QSHAfY_yXYDA

  One line per sheet row. Column A ("Primary Product in Cart") becomes the key on the left
  of `>>`, column C ("FINAL Cross-Sell Products") becomes the comma-separated list on the
  right, and every row ends in a semicolon. Column B is the older working column and is
  deliberately not used.

  Keys and values are product handles. Append `?variant=<id>` to either side to target a
  single variant instead of the whole product -- the sheet uses this for the mini sunscreen,
  which cross-sells differently to the full size. A key with a variant wins over a key with
  the bare handle, so the specific row always beats the general one.

  Order within a row is the priority order: the rail walks these left to right before it
  rotates and interleaves them, so put the strongest pairing first.

  Every handle here was checked against the live catalogue on 2026-08-05. A handle that no
  longer exists is skipped silently rather than erroring, so re-check this file after
  renaming or deleting a product.

  Usage:
  {%- capture recommendation_map -%}{% render 'cart-recommendation-map' %}{%- endcapture -%}
{% endcomment %}
